# The extension files this deriver reads a rule out of, pinned by content rather than by version.
#
# The plans declare spec 0.102, and the rules behind the expectations were read at v0.102.0, so a
# run against a checkout serving other bytes is measuring a different text. Four files here are the
# ones the corpus reaches, and deriver/calls.py takes rules from three more - boolean, string
# and datetime - which plans from producers name. The rest of extensions/ is indexed by URN but no
# rule is taken from it, so pinning it would only make an unrelated edit upstream stop this run.
#
# Regenerate with:
#   git -C <substrait checkout> ls-tree v0.102.0 extensions/ | awk '{print $3 "  " $4}'
1fb11fc89fe1663543740c0f45ca47168fc779fc  extensions/functions_aggregate_generic.yaml
d4b8db5dc1f0372e565635bfc1a9b75a1ea7d707  extensions/functions_arithmetic.yaml
50eb32dca7f4eb45ab9c36d1dad4425a3f32da0a  extensions/functions_arithmetic_decimal.yaml
dc8cd48900e09107ab5408f941c6341930b8e02a  extensions/functions_boolean.yaml
a07fd29e61dd2ed4bb4d58fd3142785d20d589c9  extensions/functions_comparison.yaml
97a18f932dd2710c4b8d60f294e834e5d7e73d3d  extensions/functions_datetime.yaml
70eca662e2b24258cb7f62c0693e3f551d46c63b  extensions/functions_string.yaml
